gaffer
=======

The in-process loop in src/gaffer/loop.py is adapted from waku-agent
(ShenSeanChen/waku-agent, MIT), specifically waku/loop/agent.py — the file
whose docstring ends "This file is the whole trick."

The DAG walk (waves of concurrent [P] nodes, serial otherwise, cycle detect)
follows the scheduler shape described for sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein
(Apache-2.0). This repo does not vendor bernstein.

Worktree merge-or-abort (dry-run, never leave a half-merge) follows the
safety contract of nekocode/agent-worktree (MIT). This repo does not vendor
agent-worktree; `gaffer doctor` will use `wt` when it is on PATH.

Memory commands shell out to gastownhall/beads (`bd`) when present.

The planner in src/gaffer/plan.py takes two things from upstream, both MIT:

  · github/spec-kit — the phase order (setup, foundational, work, polish),
    the rule that foundational blocks every later phase, and the task line
    `- [ ] [T001] Title` with `[P]` meaning "different files, no shared
    dependency, safe in one wave". Because the line format is the same, a
    tasks.md written by spec-kit is a gaffer graph with no converter.

  · ObedienceAdara/supervisor — the planner shape: ask the model for
    structured JSON instead of prose to scrape, do not fix the task count,
    and keep a deterministic template for when no model is available.

Neither is vendored. `gaffer plan` calls no API: it prints a prompt for the
agent you already have and validates whatever comes back.

The ten-slot map (G1–G4, L1–L6) is the article's inventory, not a claim
that those projects are bundled here. Install only the slots you will use.
